{
 "plan": {
  "title": "SHG Loan Performance Report",
  "subtitle": "An analysis of loan purposes, repayment statuses, and recovery trends.",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Loan Amount",
    "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Loan Amount (Rs)\") AS total_disbursed FROM shg_loan_register",
    "unit": "Rs"
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Amount Repaid",
    "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Amount Repaid (Rs)\") AS total_repaid FROM shg_loan_register",
    "unit": "Rs"
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Repayment Rate",
    "sql": "SELECT (SUM(\"Amount Repaid (Rs)\") / NULLIF(SUM(\"Loan Amount (Rs)\"), 0)) * 100 AS recovery_rate FROM shg_loan_register",
    "unit": "%"
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "pie",
    "title": "Loan Purpose Distribution",
    "sql": "SELECT Purpose AS category, COUNT(*) AS count FROM shg_loan_register GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "category",
    "y": "count"
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Loan Amount by Repayment Status",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Repayment Status\" AS status, SUM(\"Loan Amount (Rs)\") AS amount FROM shg_loan_register GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "status",
    "y": [
     "amount"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Detailed Loan Register",
    "sql": "SELECT \"SHG Name\", Purpose, \"Loan Amount (Rs)\", \"Amount Repaid (Rs)\", \"Repayment Status\" FROM shg_loan_register ORDER BY \"Loan Amount (Rs)\" DESC LIMIT 20"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The total capital disbursed through SHG loans stands at {{p1.total_disbursed}}. To date, the community has successfully repaid {{p2.total_repaid}}, resulting in an overall recovery rate of {{p3.recovery_rate}}%.\n\nLoan distribution shows that various purposes drive credit demand. The repayment status breakdown indicates the volume of capital currently held in {{p5.status}} categories. Monitoring the {{p3.recovery_rate}}% rate is essential for maintaining the revolving fund's sustainability."
 },
